UNIT divergence_of
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY package
ANCHOR rederive@6199e2cc8b75 cli/sir/v05.mjs divergenceOf — the per-language divergence verdict the lab writes to runs/<lang>/divergence.json; reproduce the code exactly, accidents included
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG divergence_of(round: i64, artifacts: list[record[artifact: text, control: bool | none, error: text | none, rungs: list[text] | none, typeCheck: record[applicable: bool, ok: bool | none] | none, _misses: list[record[slice: text | none, name: text, args: list[text], expected: text]] | none]]) -> record[round: i64, quorum: text, verdict: text, heldoutDisagree: list[record[name: text, args: list[text], expected: text, failedBy: list[text], passedBy: i64, of: i64]], frozenMissed: list[record[name: text, args: list[text], expected: text, failedBy: list[text], passedBy: i64, of: i64]] | none] | none
ENVELOPE round is an integer of magnitude at most 2^53 - 1 (the caller's round number; it is never interpreted). artifacts is
  one language's artifact list for one round, in the caller's order, each artifact a record of the fields in SIG: its name,
  whether it is the CONTROL (the shipped reconstruction), its build/run error text, its earned rungs (the texts
  "type-checked", "harness-verified", ... in any order, duplicates allowed), its static type check, and its MISSES (each
  vector it failed: the slice "frozen" or "heldout", the vector's name, its displayed arguments and its displayed expected
  value). Any text is allowed anywhere, including a slice outside the two names and a slice of none (read as "heldout",
  R6). Throws are IN scope as an observation: R5.
DEPENDS-ON none
DESCRIPTION One language's divergence verdict for one grading round: the cold quorum over the non-control artifacts that
  built and ran, and the tally of the vectors they missed — held-out misses (the SIR-ambiguity signal a HARDEN reads) apart
  from frozen misses (emitter errors). The result is none when nothing was attempted, else a record whose fields are, in
  this order: round, quorum, verdict, heldoutDisagree, frozenMissed. A tally entry's fields are, in this order: name, args,
  expected, failedBy, passedBy, of. frozenMissed is none (the key is absent in the package's own output) whenever it would
  be an empty list; heldoutDisagree is always present, possibly empty.
BEHAVIOR
R1 ATTEMPTED = the artifacts whose control is not true (false and none both count as not control), in input order. When
  ATTEMPTED is empty -> none.
R2 GRADED = the members of ATTEMPTED whose error is none, in input order. When GRADED is empty -> the record round = the
  input round, quorum = "0/0", verdict = "no-quorum", heldoutDisagree = an empty list, frozenMissed = none. Nothing else of
  the artifacts is read in this case: rungs, typeCheck and misses of an errored or control artifact never matter, and never
  throw.
R3 Any error text marks the artifact as errored, the EMPTY text included: an artifact with error "" is not GRADED.
R4 A GRADED artifact VOTES when all three hold: (a) one element of its rungs is exactly the text "harness-verified"
  (whole-text, case-sensitive equality; other elements, their order and duplicates do not matter); (b) its typeCheck is
  none, or its applicable is false, or its ok is true — so applicable true with ok false or none does not vote, and
  applicable false votes whatever ok holds; (c) it has no miss (misses none or an empty list).
  VOTES = the number of voting artifacts. quorum = the decimal digits of VOTES, then "/", then the decimal digits of the
  size of GRADED (no sign, no padding). verdict = "quorum" when VOTES is at least 2, else "no-quorum" — a fixed threshold,
  independent of the size of GRADED (2 of 5 is a quorum).
R5 When GRADED is non-empty, before any vote or tally, every GRADED artifact is checked: its rungs is none -> throws; one of
  its misses has a slice that is neither none nor exactly "frozen" or "heldout" (case-sensitive; "", "Frozen" and "held-out"
  fail; a slice of none passes) -> throws. The message is not graded. Misses of control and errored artifacts are never
  checked.
R6 TALLY(S) for a slice name S ("heldout" or "frozen") is a list built by visiting the GRADED artifacts in order and, within
  each, its misses in order (misses none is an empty list), keeping only the misses whose slice is exactly S, where a slice
  of none reads as "heldout" — it is tallied, grouped and deduped with the "heldout" misses, never with "frozen".
R7 TALLY grouping: misses are grouped by name (exact text equality). The FIRST miss seen for a name creates the entry, in
  first-seen order (never sorted), with that miss's args and expected; a later miss with the same name keeps the entry's
  args and expected (its own are discarded). Each miss appends its artifact's name to the entry's failedBy, in visit order,
  UNLESS failedBy already holds that exact text — so failedBy never repeats a name. The test is by artifact name: two
  GRADED artifacts that carry the same name count once CITED FIDELITY package — the dedupe compares names, not artifacts
  of = the size of GRADED; passedBy = of minus the length of failedBy.
R8 Otherwise (GRADED non-empty, no throw) -> the record round = the input round, quorum and verdict from R4, heldoutDisagree
  = TALLY("heldout"), frozenMissed = TALLY("frozen") when that list is non-empty, else none.
R9 round is carried to the output unchanged.
INVARIANT the result is none exactly when every artifact is a control (or there are none); of is the same in every entry and
  equals the denominator of quorum; VOTES never exceeds the size of GRADED; passedBy is never negative; an artifact that
  appears in any failedBy did not vote.
OUT-OF-DOMAIN beyond the SIG shape (not encodable, OUT of the oracle): a non-list artifacts or misses, a missing artifact name,
  a rungs value that is not a list (the code throws, as R5), a misses element that is not a record (the code throws), and a
  miss record with NO slice field at all (the code reads it as "heldout", the same as a slice of none: a record that
  predates the tag) all behave as the host makes them.
ORACLE value -> oracles/divergence_of.json  CANONICAL-SHA256 658040518ac94040bf1281fe90c0023ebc33ee33c380cf379edaa4894abca25f
SCOPE IN: R1-R9 over ENVELOPE, including the throws of R5 and the name-keyed dedupe of R7. OUT: the OUT-OF-DOMAIN shapes; the
  fields of a real artifact record the function never reads (frozen, heldout, exact, counts, narrowed, misses, extension).
PROVENANCE rederive@6199e2cc8b75 (MIT), cli/sir/v05.mjs: divergenceOf (lines 59-86). Re-cut 2026-10-27 (round 5, FINDINGS #90)
  from the pinned snapshot only; delta re-cut (round 5b, N1) on 6199e2cc8b75: a slice of none is "heldout", not a throw; the artifact shape is the one the lab's run.mjs builds.
